{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe generated artifacts from a rebar-janitor session were lost. Reconstruct the recoverable results from `~/Downloads/ChatGPT-Rebar janitor analysis-20260816-0915.md`. Decisions 1-6 require the deepest research and analysis. This is a no-code recovery: preserve evidence, distinguish transcript facts from present-day corroboration, and make uncertainty explicit.\n\nThe current skill names `.rebar-janitor/`, but this repository’s historical local-only artifact convention is `.joe-janitor/`, evidenced by tracked `.joe-janitor/tools.md` and tracker record `naive-bigheaded-wildcat`. Other git-excluded files visible in one checkout are opportunistic corroboration only: the plan does not assume that `known-fine.md` or prior `report-*.md` files survive. The deterministic output is the intentionally git-excluded local artifact `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md`. Its title and opening banner must say `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN` so future runs cannot mistake reconstructed material for an original Phase-2 record. Report-content criteria are operator-attested because repository-snapshot verifiers intentionally cannot see local-only janitor reports; checksum and structural evidence are recorded on this ticket.\n\n## Plan\n- Inventory the source transcript, its structure, and any surviving repository/tracker evidence without modifying production code.\n- Identify the rebar-janitor protocol version in effect during the transcript from its content and repository history; use the current protocol as a guide, labeling inferred mappings if the historical structure differs.\n- Reconstruct the Phase 1/2 finding and verification context needed to interpret the later decisions.\n- Recover decisions 1-6 individually, tracing evidence, prior decisions, competing remediation proposals, convergence/divergence, approval state, and ticketization status where available.\n- Cross-check material claims against the repository, ADRs, commit history, and ticket store. Perform external research when a recovered decision relies on a community-practice claim that the transcript or repository cannot substantiate; otherwise label the claim transcript-only.\n- Recover later decisions and phase summaries to the extent supported, clearly labeling gaps and confidence.\n- Write `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` with the recovery banner and record its checksum, structure, and conclusions on this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] [operator-attested] Each of decisions 1-6 has a recovered evidence record.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — Direct inspection of the git-excluded report, transcript, repository, and evidence labels; checksum and structure recorded on this ticket.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Each of decisions 1-6 states its recovered rationale.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — Direct inspection of the six report decision sections; checksum and structure recorded on this ticket.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Each of decisions 1-6 states its approval status.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — Transcript verdicts were compared to the six report decision sections and summarized on this ticket.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Each of decisions 1-6 carries an explicit confidence or uncertainty label.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — Direct inspection of all six recovery-confidence fields and explicit missing-data notes.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Claims in the report label their source as transcript, repository, tracker, or external research.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — Direct inspection of the report evidence legend and source-labeled decision records.\n- [x] [operator-attested] The report maps the current protocol’s five phases and labels any historical divergence or inferred mapping.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — Current skill blobs/history were compared to transcript structure and the report’s five phase sections.\n- [x] [operator-attested] The report explicitly names missing phase outputs.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — Direct inspection of each phase’s missing/unrecoverable output section.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Existing decision-to-ticket mappings are listed without creating duplicate remediation tickets.\n  provenance: environment=tickets-store-origin; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Exact-title rebar tracker searches and transcript no-ticket statements were recorded; no remediation ticket create command was run.\n- [x] [operator-attested] `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` exists with the `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN` banner.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Local file inspection returned 671 lines, the exact first-line banner, and SHA-256 c8a382504f15c591505df56fd55d3c5a84313f3eb57c9c4dd71153c350426cd6.\n- [x] No production-code file is modified.\n- [x] [operator-attested] A ticket comment records the recovery conclusions and exact artifact path.\n  provenance: environment=tickets-store-origin; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Rebar comments on this ticket record the artifact path, checksum, commands, outputs, run totals, phase status, and decision conclusions."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786901064926254001,"uuid":"d42ed102-5f18-4fbf-8809-02ed48ac9971"}